.\regress\artifacts\vmedefaultkill\pass1_20261020\argon_vmep1.txt:20:  1. In `vme2chip_init` (`G:4-104`), after cased `vme2_tctl` RMW (`0x60`, `G:11`, `V:87`), the guest touches population-2 registers in this exact order (all `volatile u_long` word accesses, `V:31-34`):
.\regress\artifacts\vmedefaultkill\pass1_20261020\argon_vmep1.txt:26:     - **What `vme2chip_init` does with `ctl` read from `MASTERCTL` (`0x28`) at `G:13`**: It clears bits `23:16` (`~(0xff << 16)`, `G:30`, `V:36, V:57`), ORs `(0x0e | 0x80) << 16 = 0x008e0000` (`G:31-32`, `V:39, V:51`), clears bits `31:24` (`~(0xff << 24)`, `G:45`, `V:35, V:57`), ORs `0x0e << 24 = 0x0e000000` (`G:46-47`, `V:51`), writes `ctl` (`0x0e8e0000` when the read returned `0`) to `vme2_masterctl` at `G:55`, and overwrites `ctl = vme2->vme2_gcsrctl` at `G:57`[cite: 2]. No branch depends on `ctl`, so reading `0` from `MASTERCTL` does not change guest control flow in `vme2chip_init`; however, in the emulator, the read at `G:13` sets bit `0x28 >> 2 = 10` in `d->warned_unimpl` (`B:415`), suppressing the write announce at `G:55`[cite: 1, 2].
.\regress\artifacts\vmedefaultkill\pass1_20261020\argon_vmep1.txt:27:  2. In `vme2abort` (`G:131-145`), the guest touches:
.\regress\artifacts\vmedefaultkill\pass1_20261020\argon_vmep1.txt:30:     - **What `vme2abort` does when `vme2_irqstat` (`0x68`) reads `0`**: Because `VME2_IRQ_AB = 0x40000000` (`V:96`), `!(0 & 0x40000000)` is true (`G:137`), so `vme2abort` prints `"vme2abort irq not set\n"` (`G:138`) and executes `return 0;` (`G:139`)[cite: 2]. Reading `0` from `IRQSTAT` makes `vme2->vme2_irqclr = VME2_IRQ_AB` (`G:142`) and `nmihand(frame)` (`G:143`) unreachable in the guest[cite: 2]. Because `B:475` explicitly places *"the guest's abort-handler consequence"* on the detector's `NOT CLAIMED` list (`S3` ruled `DECLINE` rather than `IMPLEMENT` for `IRQSTAT`), no detector row should demand `IRQSTAT != 0`, but the sketch's code comment at `B:400-402` is inaccurate[cite: 1, 2].
.\regress\artifacts\vmedefaultkill\pass1_20261020\argon_vmep1.txt:32:FLAG: B:400-402, G:13, G:55, G:137-142 -- The sketch comment claims `vme2chip_init()` only writes `MASTERCTL` (omitting the prior read at `G:13` that consumes `MASTERCTL`'s latch bit) and claims `vme2abort()` writes `IRQCLR` (whereas serving `0` on `IRQSTAT` at `G:137` forces `vme2abort()` to return `0` at `G:139` without reaching `IRQCLR` at `G:142`).
